# What must not enter the Docker build context.
#
# There was no .dockerignore, so `COPY . .` sent everything: 388 MB of
# node_modules, the host's dist/, backups, and any .env sitting in the
# repository. Three separate problems:
#
#   1. The builder runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and then `COPY . .`
#      overwrites that node_modules with the host's. The container ends up
#      building against whatever the host happened to have — a different
#      platform, possibly a different resolution — rather than the lockfile it
#      just installed from.
#
#   2. Secrets. `.env` holds the database password, JWT secret, and Matrix
#      shared secret. Copied into a build layer it stays in the image history
#      even if a later stage doesn't reference it.
#
#   3. Speed. Sending 388 MB per build, on every build.

# Dependencies — the image installs its own from the lockfile.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Build output — the builder produces this itself. Copying the host's in
# risks shipping a stale bundle if anything downstream skips the rebuild.
dist
build
desktop/dist
desktop/src-tauri/target

# Secrets and generated configuration.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dendrite/dendrite.yaml
dendrite/matrix_key.pem
ssl

# Backups contain every message and every secret.
backups

# Not needed to build or run the server.
.git
.github
site
docs
desktop
identity
*.md
!README.md

# Local noise.
.vscode
.idea
logs
*.log
coverage
.DS_Store
